{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Simple series circuits: parts and building","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1d3557","font":"Trebuchet MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Cell"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A cell stores energy and pushes electricity around a circuit. It has a positive and a negative end."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Series circuit"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A circuit where all the parts are joined in one single loop, so the electricity has only one path to follow."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which part of a circuit provides the energy?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A bulb","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A cell","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A wire","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is the job of a switch in a circuit?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"To make the bulb brighter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"To store energy for later","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"To open or close the circuit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which part makes a buzzing sound when the circuit is complete?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A buzzer","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A cell","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"A switch","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"What must a circuit form for the bulb to light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"A broken gap","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"A complete loop","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"A pile of wires","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which symbol means a cell in a circuit diagram?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"A circle with a cross inside","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"A long line and a short line","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Your group wants to light a bulb. Do you test the circuit with a switch first, or join the wires straight to the cell?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Add a switch first","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Join the wires straight to the cell","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"You add a switch and close it. The bulb lights up, and your group cheers. The switch lets you control the circuit."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-t","content":"The wires touch the cell but do not form a loop with the bulb, so nothing lights. Your group tries again with a complete loop."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"You finished the series circuits lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You now know the cell, wires, bulbs, switches and buzzers, and how to build a complete loop."}],"actions":[]}}
